// The item cases of design 3.6: an accept case and a reject case for each item of design 5.4
// that rule (a) uses, in the format of HAND. `accept` keeps the rule, and `reject` breaks it at a
// store that a run reaches with a live allocation. The places, `move` and `null` are the operands
// and the gen rules, `fresh` the `alloc` into a pointer local, `call` the call, `pointer`,
// `straight`, `key` and `global_store` the kill rules of a store, `join` and `loop` the
// terminators, `held` the held address of a store whose right side calls, `zero` the zero
// aggregate, `order` the gen of a `move` argument before the kill of its call, `copy` and
// `fresh_join` the end and the join of freshness, and `leaving` a store behind a second deref.
// Four sites are false rejects of V1. The accept case of `held` stores after a call, which kills
// the fact of `q->a` (kill rule 5 of D17.11). In `copy`, `leaving` and `fresh_join`, the store
// through the alias has no fact for its place, and the run finds the place empty. `test_null`,
// `test_loop` and `test_alias` hold the tests against null (D17.11 gen rule 6): the accept cases
// store in the arm where a test of `==`, of `!` or of a loop finds null, and the reject cases store
// after a call in the arm, after the edge out of `while (x == null)`, and after a store through a
// second pointer to the same object.
// The count of the lines of ITEMS.
u64 ITEM_LINES = 570;

